   129	
   130	## Tone and compliance notes
   131	- Medical advertising: no guarantees, use phrases like "clinical averages", "results vary", "your surgeon will advise", "many patients experience"
   132	- AHPRA/TGA: no testimonials, no before/after claims, no guaranteed outcomes; weight loss percentages (e.g. 60–70% excess weight) must be framed as "many patients" or "clinical averages", never as guaranteed individual results
   133	- Voice: plain-language, confident, honest; avoid hype; the reader has likely done significant research — do not talk down to them
   134	- Reader: a Perth adult who already knows what bariatric surgery is; they are comparing providers and want to trust this team with something significant; credentialism (FRACS, SJOG hospitals, 20+ years) matters here
   135	- The page should answer "why OSWA" without ever asking the question

