content-briefs/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:132:- AHPRA/TGA: no testimonials, no before/after claims, no guaranteed outcomes; weight loss percentages (e.g. 60–70% excess weight) must be framed as "many patients" or "clinical averages", never as guaranteed individual results
content-briefs/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:134:- Reader: a Perth adult who already knows what bariatric surgery is; they are comparing providers and want to trust this team with something significant; credentialism (FRACS, SJOG hospitals, 20+ years) matters here
content-reviews/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:5:**Why:** Prescription-medicine references, safety wording, Medicare/private-health certainty, hospital verification and hub-page structure need correction before publication.
content-reviews/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:7:**Length:** current body 2,091 words vs brief target 1,200-1,500 words, including FAQs.
content-reviews/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:11:1. **TGA prescription-medicine risk: semaglutide is named in public-facing promotional copy**
content-reviews/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:13:> Medical weight management: non-surgical weight loss treatment pathways including GLP-1 medications (such as semaglutide) and structured dietitian-led programs.
content-reviews/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:17:Why it matters: TGA states that "advertising prescription medicines to the public is prohibited" and specifically calls out weight-loss injections in compliance action, so naming semaglutide on a promotional service page is a publish risk: https://www.tga.gov.au/news/media-releases/tga-releases-new-guidance-advertising-restrictions-prescription-medicines.
content-reviews/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:19:2. **The FAQ promotes GLP-1 treatment without enough balance [also fix the brief]**
content-reviews/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:21:> Medical weight management, including GLP-1 medications and dietitian-led programs, is a genuine and effective option for many people, and our team offers this alongside surgical pathways.
content-reviews/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:37:> Medicare rebates apply to most bariatric procedures when eligibility criteria are met, and private health insurance with a gold-tier or equivalent policy covers the hospital and theatre component.
content-reviews/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:41:Why it matters: The blocker is the certainty and breadth of "most bariatric procedures" and "covers the hospital and theatre component", because coverage needs item-specific, policy-specific and gap-aware wording.
content-reviews/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:43:5. **The opening section keeps a GLP-1 class reference [also fix the brief]**
content-reviews/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:45:> Our dedicated patient care team also offers GLP-1 medical weight management, dietetic support, and exercise physiology in-clinic at Booragoon and Greenfields.
content-reviews/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:49:Why it matters: If only later GLP-1 references are removed, a prescription-medicine class reference still survives in the opening section; the writer followed the brief's medical-weight-management direction as instructed, so the brief also needs correction.
