### G5 — brief corrections applied

The brief has been edited directly. The changed directions are:

- The risks instruction no longer says that keyhole techniques and experienced surgeons “make these procedures safe for most suitable candidates”; it now requires small-incision description without comparative safety, pain or recovery claims.
- The BMI summary and bullets now state the MBS rule: BMI 40 or above, or BMI 35–39.9 with at least one major obesity-related condition — always subject to individual clinical assessment; BMI below 35 does not meet the MBS threshold.
- Procedure bullets no longer promise comparative weight loss, “preferred” status, substantial outcomes or least weight loss; they direct the surgeon to explain individual risks, benefits and follow-up.
- The cost direction now uses conditional Medicare/private-health wording, requires any range or estimate to be discussed at consultation, and keeps dollar figures out.
- The FAQ direction now includes Perth cost, Medicare coverage, the 30/30 rule, who may not meet MBS or clinical suitability requirements, 10-year variation and how to assess a surgeon.
- The GLP-1/active-ingredient wording is marked as pending TGA/legal review; if retained, use active-ingredient/class names only and no brand names.

Verification flags: hospital identity and affiliations remain to be verified with the client; the GLP-1/medical-weight-management advertising policy remains pending; confirm current MBS/referral/insurer details before publish.

## Batch-1 completion report

The brief direction now:

- Describes laparoscopic techniques without saying they “make these procedures safe for most suitable candidates,” and prohibits comparative safety, pain or recovery claims.
- States the MBS rule as BMI 40 or above, or BMI 35–39.9 with a major obesity-related condition — always subject to individual clinical assessment; BMI below 35 does not meet the MBS threshold.
- Avoids comparative weight-loss, “preferred” and outcome-assurance wording in the procedure bullets.
- Uses conditional Medicare/private-health wording, requires any range or estimate to be discussed at consultation, and keeps dollar figures out.
- Includes Perth cost, Medicare coverage, the 30/30 rule, who may not meet MBS or clinical suitability requirements, 10-year variation and how to assess a surgeon in the FAQ plan.
- Marks the GLP-1/active-ingredient wording as OPEN — pending TGA/legal decision; if retained, use active-ingredient/class names only and no brand names.

Verification flags: hospital identity and affiliations remain to be verified; the GLP-1/medical-weight-management advertising policy remains pending; confirm current MBS, referral and insurer details before publication.

